{
  "concept": "For 0 < x < π/2, the areas sin x/2 ≤ x/2 ≤ tan x/2 sandwich the circular sector between two triangles, which forces sin x / x → 1 as x → 0.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "Left panel: coordinate axes with arrowheads (x-axis horizontal, y-axis vertical), origin at center",
    "Left panel: blue unit circle centered at origin",
    "Left panel: red radius from origin to point (cos x, sin x) extended as a ray to (1, tan x)",
    "Left panel: red dot and label '(1, 0)' at the point where circle meets positive x-axis",
    "Left panel: red dot and label '(cos x, sin x)' with leader arrow to the point on the circle",
    "Left panel: red dot and label '(1, tan x)' at the top of the vertical tangent line x = 1",
    "Left panel: dashed red vertical segment from (1,0) up to (1, tan x)",
    "Left panel: dashed red chord from (cos x, sin x) down to (1, 0)",
    "Left panel: blue highlighted arc from (1,0) to (cos x, sin x)",
    "Left panel: small arc arrow at origin labeled 'x' marking the angle",
    "Left panel: curly brace under the segment from origin to (1,0) labeled '1'",
    "Right panel A: large right triangle with base 1 (labeled) and vertical leg labeled 'tan x', pink fill, red outline, dashed blue arc inside, angle arrow labeled 'x'",
    "Right panel B: circular sector of radius 1 and angle x, pink fill, red straight edges, blue curved arc, base labeled '1', angle arrow labeled 'x'",
    "Right panel C: small triangle with base 1, apex at (cos x, sin x), pink fill, red outline, dashed blue arc bulging outside, dashed red vertical segment showing height, brace labeled 'sin x', angle arrow labeled 'x'",
    "Caption row: 'Area of triangle  ≥  Area of sector  ≥  Area of triangle'",
    "Formula row: 'tan x / 2  ≥  x / 2  ≥  sin x / 2'",
    "Derived inequality annotation: 'cos x ≤ sin x / x ≤ 1 / cos x'",
    "Numeric readout of the three area values for the current x"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "angleX",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "angle x (radians)",
      "range": [0.05, 1.5, 0.01],
      "default": 0.7,
      "teaches": "As x shrinks, the outer triangle, sector, and inner triangle converge in both shape and area, so the bounds on sin x / x close in on 1."
    },
    {
      "id": "overlayMode",
      "type": "toggle",
      "label": "Panel layout",
      "options": ["Side by side", "Overlaid"],
      "default": "Side by side",
      "teaches": "Stacking the three regions on one set of axes makes the nesting inner triangle ⊂ sector ⊂ outer triangle literally visible, which is why the areas are ordered."
    },
    {
      "id": "regionFocus",
      "type": "click",
      "teaches": "Clicking a region or its caption isolates one area and its formula, connecting each picture to its algebraic expression tan x/2, x/2, or sin x/2."
    },
    {
      "id": "squeezePlay",
      "type": "animation",
      "label": "Let x → 0",
      "loop": true,
      "teaches": "Watching x sweep toward zero shows cos x and 1/cos x both collapsing to 1, squeezing sin x / x between them."
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "The unit circle setup",
      "narration": "A single angle x produces three key points: (1,0) on the axis, (cos x, sin x) on the circle, and (1, tan x) on the tangent line. Drag the slider to see all three move together.",
      "state": { "angleX": 0.7, "overlayMode": "Side by side" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Three regions, three areas",
      "narration": "The same angle defines a big triangle of area tan x/2, a sector of area x/2, and a small triangle of area sin x/2. Click any caption to highlight its region and formula.",
      "state": { "angleX": 0.7, "overlayMode": "Side by side" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Nesting makes the order obvious",
      "narration": "Overlay the three regions: the small triangle sits inside the sector, which sits inside the big triangle. Containment forces sin x/2 ≤ x/2 ≤ tan x/2.",
      "state": { "angleX": 0.7, "overlayMode": "Overlaid" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Shrinking the angle",
      "narration": "Reduce x and the three nested regions become nearly indistinguishable — their areas crowd together.",
      "state": { "angleX": 0.25, "overlayMode": "Overlaid" }
    },
    {
      "title": "The squeeze",
      "narration": "Dividing the inequality by sin x/2 gives cos x ≤ sin x/x ≤ 1/cos x. As x → 0 both bounds go to 1, so sin x / x must go to 1.",
      "state": { "angleX": 0.08, "overlayMode": "Overlaid" }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "The sector is literally trapped between two triangles built from the same angle, so its area x/2 is trapped between sin x/2 and tan x/2 — and as the trap tightens, sin x / x has nowhere to go but 1.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Two-zone layout. Left zone: black axes with arrowheads, a blue unit circle centered at the origin, radius drawn in red from origin to the circle point, extended to the vertical tangent line at x = 1; the segment from (1,0) up to (1, tan x) and the chord from (cos x, sin x) to (1,0) are dashed red; small dots in red at the three labeled points with serif labels '(1, tan x)', '(cos x, sin x)' (with leader arrow), '(1, 0)'; a small curved arrow at the origin labeled 'x'; a curly brace beneath the unit-length base labeled '1'. Right zone: three shapes in a row, all sharing a base of length 1 on a common baseline, pink/salmon fill with red outlines; leftmost is the tall right triangle with vertical leg labeled 'tan x' and a dashed blue arc cutting inside it; middle is the sector with a solid blue arc as its curved edge; rightmost is the short triangle whose apex is the circle point, with a dashed blue arc bulging just outside the slanted side, a thin dashed red vertical height line, and a brace labeled 'sin x'. Each shape carries a small angle arrow labeled 'x' at its left vertex and '1' under its base. Two caption rows in serif type below: 'Area of triangle ≥ Area of sector ≥ Area of triangle' and the stacked fractions 'tan x/2 ≥ x/2 ≥ sin x/2'. In Overlaid mode the three shapes are drawn concentrically on one origin with graded pink opacity (darkest = smallest triangle) so the containment reads at a glance, and a live readout shows numeric values for tan x/2, x/2, sin x/2 plus the derived chain cos x ≤ sin x/x ≤ 1/cos x. Highlighted region on click gets a saturated red stroke and its formula badge enlarges; non-selected regions fade to light gray-pink."
}

